2. Data
-------

Most of this repository by size is not code and is not the maintainer's work.
Approximately 658 MB of the tree is data, against roughly 16 MB of code:

    data/egzamin-osmoklasisty/   exam result spreadsheets published by CIE
                                 (Centrum Informatyczne Edukacji), committed
                                 verbatim and unmodified, so that every
                                 published number can be traced to its source
    docs/geo/                    PRG administrative boundary polygons,
                                 produced by GUGiK, obtained through CIE's
                                 asset bundle at mapa.wyniki.edu.pl
    docs/data/, output/          values computed from the CIE data by the
                                 pipeline in this repository

The MIT licence covers the pipeline that computes those outputs. It does not
purport to license the source data, which belongs to its publishers.

PRG boundary polygons. Produced by GUGiK and, under the Prawo geodezyjne i
kartograficzne, supplied free of charge with NO LICENCE ISSUED for them at all
(Art. 40a ust. 2 pkt 1 lit. a; Art. 40c ust. 5). One condition attaches:
Art. 40c ust. 3 requires the source to be stated in published works, which this
project does on its help page and in the map's attribution control.

    Note that dane.gov.pl labels this dataset "CC BY 4.0". Treat that as
    corroboration that the data is open, not as a licence grant: the statute
    provides that no licence is issued, so no CC BY licence exists to rely on.
    The same record elsewhere calls it "Other (Public Domain)", which is a
    further reason to rest on the statute rather than on the portal's label.

CIE exam spreadsheets. Public sector information, re-usable for any purpose.
CIE published no re-use conditions on the channel these files were taken from,
and the applicable statutory default where a body states none is unconditional
and free of charge.

    This is a reading of the statute, not a written permission obtained from
    the publisher, and it should be treated as such. Two things in particular
    remain open: the rule deeming silence to mean unconditional re-use is
    written for the Biuletyn Informacji Publicznej and the national data
    portal, and mapa.wyniki.edu.pl is neither; and the sui generis database
    right is a separate right from copyright, which nothing here resolves.

    The files are committed byte-identical to what was downloaded, and
    data/egzamin-osmoklasisty/SOURCES.csv records the exact URL and retrieval
    date of each one. They would be removed on request from the publisher.

Sources are credited on the project's help page, under "Dane i zakres" and
"Inne zrodla i kod". If you intend to reuse the data itself rather than the
code, check the publishers' current terms directly rather than relying on this
file.


3. Third-party components loaded at run time
--------------------------------------------

None of the following is redistributed in this repository; the pages fetch each
from its own host when a visitor opens them.

    Leaflet 1.9.4 and Leaflet.markercluster 1.5.3, from unpkg.com, each under
